    <innernamespace refid="namespacePduNode">PduNode</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>PDU monitoring node — the whole node in two calls (#216). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A PDU sketch is just: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="preprocessor">#include<sp/>&lt;<ref refid="PduNode_8h" kindref="compound">PduNode.h</ref>&gt;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">void</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>setup()<sp/>{<sp/><ref refid="namespaceSTM32Board_1a3c18d8a23e0bc42e5ff7e7e5f1e11587" kindref="member">STM32Board::setDebug</ref>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">true</highlight><highlight class="normal">);<sp/><ref refid="namespacePduNode_1acdbc21507ef00a33b9ffde79fc5cc9bd" kindref="member">PduNode::setup</ref>();<sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">void</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>loop()<sp/><sp/>{<sp/><ref refid="namespacePduNode_1a6765fd2baba5c59d747d3a96b57a4cdf" kindref="member">PduNode::loop</ref>();<sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> with <computeroutput>-DNODE_ID=N</computeroutput> in platformio.ini. What runs:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Node status</bold> — HB_n / HEALTH_n (board kind PDU, #344) / master-loss watchdog via <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol_1aee035f550086e47e9c533b9f547687f9" kindref="member">CANProtocol::serviceNodeStatus()</ref>. Rail and thermal faults reach HEALTH_n.faultId through the FaultSource registry.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Sampling</bold> — the four rail channels every PDU_SAMPLE_US (1 kHz target); the NTC and Vrefint every 100 ms. Faults are held clear for PDU_BOOT_BLANK_MS after boot.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Telemetry</bold> — one TELEM_n frame per second, rotating PDU_RAIL_12V → PDU_RAIL_5V → PDU_STATUS; a page whose flags change goes out at once (≤ 1 per 100 ms per page); SYNC_REQ sends all three pages immediately.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Calibration</bold> — DiagSerial (115200) commands, one per line: <computeroutput>CAL SHOW</computeroutput> · <computeroutput>CAL VDDA &lt;mV&gt;</computeroutput> (DMM reading of the 3V3 rail) · <computeroutput>CAL ZERO</computeroutput> (no load connected) · <computeroutput>CAL CLEAR</computeroutput> · <computeroutput>RAW</computeroutput> (live readings + scan rate). Stored per board in the reserved flash page (PduCalStore).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Rail faults are reported to the host only (TELEM_n flags + HEALTH_n.faultId). The status LEDs follow every other node — CAN / link state plus the master-loss WARNING — and don&apos;t change for rail faults (FirmwarePlan D14). The board&apos;s power LEDs (D3 12 V / D4 5 V / D5 3V3) are passive, wired to their rails, and show rail presence only — this firmware never drives them.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="copyright"><para>GPL-2.0-only — see Firmware/LICENSE </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
